=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"La Isleta Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":28.17408,"lo":-15.41897,"d":3568,"ds":"La Isleta Lighthouse (Spanish: Faro de La Isleta) is an active 19th century lighthouse on the Spanish island of Gran Canaria in the Canary islands. The lighthouse has been constructed on the rocky peninsula of La Isleta, which overlooks the Port of Las Palmas to the north of the city of Las Palmas, the capital of Gran Canaria.","wpu":"La Isleta Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Faro_de_La_Isleta_3710.jpg/960px-Faro_de_La_Isleta_3710.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Palacete Rodriguez Quegles","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":28.105657,"lo":-15.418439,"d":4044,"ds":"The Palacete Rodríguez Quegles is a mansion, or small palace, in Las Palmas, capital of Gran Canaria island, in the Canary Islands of Spain. It was built around 1901 as an elaborate residence for a wealthy businessman, then in 1972 sold to the city of Las Palmas for use as a music conservatory. The restored building is now a cultural center.","wpu":"Palacete Rodriguez Quegles","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Palacete_Quegles_04.jpg/960px-Palacete_Quegles_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Diocese of Canarias","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":28.1008,"lo":-15.4151,"d":4606,"ds":"The Diocese of Canarias or Diocese Canariense-Rubicense (Latin: Dioecesis Canariensis) is a Latin diocese of the Catholic Church located in the Canary Islands in the ecclesiastical province of Seville in Spain. The dioceses includes the islands of Gran Canaria, Fuerteventura and Lanzarote (Oriental Province).","wpu":"Diocese of Canarias","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Catedral_Santa_Ana.jpg/960px-Catedral_Santa_Ana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Atlantic Center of Modern Art","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":28.10097,"lo":-15.413472,"d":4607,"ds":"The Atlantic Center for Modern Art (Spanish: Centro Atlántico de Arte Moderno) (CAAM) is a contemporary art museum in the Canary Islands, Spain. It is in Vegueta in Las Palmas, the capital city of Gran Canaria. The building was designed by the architect Francisco Javier Sáenz de Oiza, retaining the façade of two older neoclassical houses.","wpu":"Atlantic Center of Modern Art","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Centro_Atl%C3%A1ntico_de_Arte_Moderno.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Museo Canario","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":28.099832,"lo":-15.415867,"d":4706,"ds":"El Museo Canario (English: the Canarian Museum) is an archeological museum in Las Palmas, the capital city of Gran Canaria in the Canary Islands. It is dedicated to the pre-colonial history of the Canary Islands.","wpu":"Museo Canario","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Museo_Canario.JPG/960px-Museo_Canario.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Jardín Botánico Canario Viera y Clavijo","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":28.0636,"lo":-15.4633,"d":9697,"ds":"Jardín Botánico Canario Viera y Clavijo is the full name of the botanical garden on Gran Canaria, one of the Canary Islands. \"Jardín Botánico Canario\" means \"Botanical Garden of the Canaries\", while the additional words \"Viera y Clavijo\" honor the pioneering Spanish cleric and scholar José Viera y Clavijo (1731–1813), who attempted to found a botanical garden in the Canary Islands in the late eighteenth century.","wpu":"Jardín Botánico Canario Viera y Clavijo","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Jos%C3%A9_de_Viera_y_Clavijo.jpg/960px-Jos%C3%A9_de_Viera_y_Clavijo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Gran Canaria (UK: , US: ; Spanish: [ɡɾaŋ kaˈnaɾja] ), also Grand Canary Island, is the third-largest and second-most-populous island of the Canary Islands, a Spanish archipelago off the Atlantic coast of Northwest Africa. As of 2023 the island had a population of 862,893 that constitutes approximately 40% of the population of the archipelago. Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, the capital of the island, is the largest city of the Canary Islands and the ninth-largest city of Spain.","wpu":"Gran Canaria","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/55/Gran_Canaria_Sentinel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}